# C38 remediation after attempt-02 (9/8/9/8/8, no blockers: accepted at 8, one required fix)

Attempt-02 passes the chunk bar (8 in every dimension, no blockers; `attempt-02/acceptance.md`). Its one required fix is remediated here for the push to 9 (D034: a new generation, attempt-03, later chunks not reopened).

| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 [P2] the v2 Project, MCP, History and Sign-in panels collapsed an unknown delivery into "That was not done" (and the Project panel gave every refusal the folder-validation wording), so a permission change, an MCP sign-out, a permanent deletion or a Harness sign-out that may already have happened read as not done, inviting an unsafe retry | `actionOutcomeText`/`notConfirmedText` (`v2/harness/text.ts`): an unknown delivery is shown as "Not confirmed: <the action>. The desktop did not confirm it and it may have been done. Check <the panel's state> before trying again."; a refusal says its own reason (`outcomeMessage`) unless the panel has specific wording for it (the eight-server limit, the sign-in-already-running line, the company sign-in form's field errors); a failed delivery is "not done". Every send in the four panels names its action (allowing changes in this folder, signing out of <server>, deleting the conversation, signing out, …). Nothing is resent by the page: the next snapshot is the word on what happened. | `v2/harness/text.ts`, `v2/harness/panels/{project,mcp,history,sign-in}.tsx` |
| R1 acceptance: tests through the v2 imports for lost receipts of these actions, with later snapshots establishing whether the change occurred, no nonexecution asserted, no resubmission | One workflow test drives the four panels with every receipt for `setHarnessWrite`, `signOutMcpServer`, `deleteHarnessHistory` and `signOutHarness` lost (`DeliveryOutcomeUnknown`): each shows its Not confirmed line naming the action and never "not done"; the control follows the snapshot, not the click; the next snapshot (the permission applied, the server signed out, the conversation gone, the account gone) settles the state; the page's dispatch count does not grow after it (only the client's own single resend is allowed); a real refusal (`busy`) then says its own reason. The project panel's earlier refusal expectation now reads the refusal's reason rather than the folder wording. | `v2/harness/harness.test.tsx` ("keeps a lost receipt as Not confirmed in the v2 panels…", attempt-02 R1) |
| O2 the parity notes' approval paragraph named the originally approved bundle as the gate's | The paragraph distinguishes the owner's look (the 7d61d9cc composites) from the gate's composites, regenerated by the native script from the bundle `parity/bundle.json` names on every run. | `evidence/C38/parity/notes.md` |
| O1 duplicate initial history/catalog reads | Not changed in this generation (optional; the reads are idempotent and the later lease supersedes the earlier). | — |

